{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "עמוני ומואבי", :translit "ammoni umoavi", :gloss "an Ammonite and a Moabite"} {:he "ממזר", :translit "mamzer", :gloss "a mamzer"} {:he "שבנות לוט נבעלו לאביהן", :translit "shebenot lot niv'alu le'avihan", :gloss "for the daughters of Lot were violated by their father"} {:he "וילדו ממזרים", :translit "vayaledu mamzerim", :gloss "and bore mamzerim"} {:he "והנקבות מותרות", :translit "vehanekevot mutarot", :gloss "and the females are permitted"} {:he "שהם נתכוונו לדבר מצוה", :translit "shehem nitkavnu ledavar mitzvah", :gloss "for they intended for a matter of mitzvah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (smikhut) of the phrases 'ammoni umoavi' and 'mamzer' in adjacent verse-contexts to derive the legal identification."}], :frame {:text "The daughters of Lot, fearing that no men remained alive after the destruction of Sodom, got their father drunk and lay with him to preserve humanity; from these unions were born the ancestors of Ammon and Moab (Genesis 19:30–38). The term 'mamzer' is defined halakhically as the offspring of a union punishable by karet or execution; incest between father and daughter falls under karet (Sanhedrin 76b; Yevamot 76b), so the males of Ammon and Moab descended from that union bear the status of mamzerim.", :sources ["Genesis 19:30–38" "Sanhedrin 76b" "Yevamot 76b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (smikhut) of the phrases 'ammoni umoavi' and 'mamzer' in adjacent verse-contexts to derive the legal identification.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:38:32.257060967Z", :model "glm-5.2"}